spirv: OpenCL program-scope const variables with initializers

OpenCL C 2.0 puts program-scope const variables in __global (CrossWorkgroup), with an
initializer and the Constant decoration; vtn failed on them ("Initializer for
CrossWorkgroup variable not yet supported"). Nothing can write them, so they are made
constant data, as UniformConstant variables are. Pixel's camera HAL has such programs.

diff --git a/src/compiler/spirv/vtn_variables.c b/src/compiler/spirv/vtn_variables.c
index d6ba3d18154..9a7d2ab10ef 100644
--- a/src/compiler/spirv/vtn_variables.c
+++ b/src/compiler/spirv/vtn_variables.c
@@ -2147,6 +2147,15 @@ vtn_create_variable(struct vtn_builder *b, struct vtn_value *val,
    vtn_assert(ptr_type->base_type == vtn_base_type_pointer);
    struct vtn_type *without_array = vtn_type_without_array(data_type);
 
+   /* OpenCL C 2.0 program-scope const variables are __global (CrossWorkgroup), with an
+    * initializer and the Constant decoration. Nothing can write them: they are constant
+    * data, as UniformConstant variables are.
+    */
+   if (storage_class == SpvStorageClassCrossWorkgroup && initializer &&
+       initializer->value_type == vtn_value_type_constant &&
+       vtn_has_decoration(b, val, SpvDecorationConstant))
+      storage_class = SpvStorageClassUniformConstant;
+
    enum vtn_variable_mode mode;
    nir_variable_mode nir_mode;
    mode = vtn_storage_class_to_mode(b, storage_class, without_array, &nir_mode);
